<article class="env-corollary" id="6D4523">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/6D4523">Corollary <span data-tag="6D4523">5.5.9.3</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a small category which admits finite products, and let ${\mathbf A}$ be as in Proposition <a href="/tag/7CFD34" data-tag="7CFD34">5.5.9.2</a>. Then the natural map $\Nerve ( {\mathbf A}^{\circ } ) \rightarrow \calP _{\Sigma }( \Nerve (\calC )^{op} )$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. </p>
